        "end_line": 38,
        "explicit_terminal_LF_map": null,
        "formula": "\\|x\\|^2+\\|Kx\\|^2=\\|Dx\\|^2.",
        "literal_BODY_match": true,
        "module_path": "E:/Samplinglib/AutoSamplingTheory/TechnicalLemmas/Analysis/HilbertCorrectorBound.lean",
        "slug": "hilbert-sharp-quadratic-corrector-bound",
        "span_RAW_bytes": 529,
        "span_RAW_sha256": "49b2427ff3ad0df9fbc373dabc9a557064dd2419cfcd84494111e45ea0d36c33",
        "start_line": 29,
        "step": 1,
        "text": "Evaluate I+K²=D² against x. Selfadjointness moves the outer K and D across the inner product.",
        "title": "Turn the operator square into a norm identity",
        "whole_source_RAW_sha256": "832e68d649c4f6a0c342a476a9d5a7bc5c95d3098abfe41c077cbabc5d51158a"
      },
      {
        "body_start_line": 28,
        "code_RAW_bytes": 596,
        "code_RAW_sha256": "9f867c93bb6aedab9ba178fd1922f2dd9bb3a89cd9441682609167d73178ab84",
        "end_line": 50,
        "explicit_terminal_LF_map": null,
        "formula": "\\|u-Kv\\|^2+\\|Ku+v\\|^2=\\|Du\\|^2+\\|Dv\\|^2,\\quad E=\\langle u-Kv,u\\rangle-\\langle Ku+v,v\\rangle.",
        "literal_BODY_match": true,
        "module_path": "E:/Samplinglib/AutoSamplingTheory/TechnicalLemmas/Analysis/HilbertCorrectorBound.lean",
        "slug": "hilbert-sharp-quadratic-corrector-bound",
        "span_RAW_bytes": 596,
        "span_RAW_sha256": "9f867c93bb6aedab9ba178fd1922f2dd9bb3a89cd9441682609167d73178ab84",
        "start_line": 39,
        "step": 2,
        "text": "Use the sum of the two squared component norms. Symmetry cancels the mixed terms; this is the Hilbert sum energy, without a product max-norm assertion.",
        "title": "Cancel the two block cross terms",
        "whole_source_RAW_sha256": "832e68d649c4f6a0c342a476a9d5a7bc5c95d3098abfe41c077cbabc5d51158a"
      },
      {
        "body_start_line": 28,
        "code_RAW_bytes": 660,
        "code_RAW_sha256": "86718d728669a29444e103a04b1e6c2b4004d7c4dc19704e4e4207952fc6c8cd",
        "end_line": 63,
        "explicit_terminal_LF_map": null,
        "formula": "|E|\\le\\|u-Kv\\|\\|u\\|+\\|Ku+v\\|\\|v\\|,\\quad T\\le c^2 S.",
        "literal_BODY_match": true,
        "module_path": "E:/Samplinglib/AutoSamplingTheory/TechnicalLemmas/Analysis/HilbertCorrectorBound.lean",
        "slug": "hilbert-sharp-quadratic-corrector-bound",
        "span_RAW_bytes": 660,
        "span_RAW_sha256": "86718d728669a29444e103a04b1e6c2b4004d7c4dc19704e4e4207952fc6c8cd",
        "start_line": 51,
        "step": 3,
        "text": "Triangle inequality and the inner-product bound control E. The operator norm controls each D component.",
        "title": "Bound the quadratic form and block energy",
        "whole_source_RAW_sha256": "832e68d649c4f6a0c342a476a9d5a7bc5c95d3098abfe41c077cbabc5d51158a"
      },
      {
        "body_start_line": 28,
        "code_RAW_bytes": 653,
        "code_RAW_sha256": "92436031b474a6512a8e872f49c541cb010770dc1b196df96782448a033c0a5b",
        "end_line": 75,
        "explicit_terminal_LF_map": null,
        "formula": "(ab+de)^2\\le(a^2+d^2)(b^2+e^2),\\quad E^2\\le S T\\le c^2S^2.",
        "literal_BODY_match": true,
        "module_path": "E:/Samplinglib/AutoSamplingTheory/TechnicalLemmas/Analysis/HilbertCorrectorBound.lean",
        "slug": "hilbert-sharp-quadratic-corrector-bound",
        "span_RAW_bytes": 653,
        "span_RAW_sha256": "92436031b474a6512a8e872f49c541cb010770dc1b196df96782448a033c0a5b",
        "start_line": 64,
        "step": 4,
        "text": "The scalar inequality follows from a single nonnegative square. Combine with the block energy bound, keeping S nonnegative.",
        "title": "Apply two-component Cauchy-Schwarz",
        "whole_source_RAW_sha256": "832e68d649c4f6a0c342a476a9d5a7bc5c95d3098abfe41c077cbabc5d51158a"
      },
      {
        "body_start_line": 28,
        "code_RAW_bytes": 354,
        "code_RAW_sha256": "0b0fe5736aabe70a55a7368aaff5e859c6b702082d780ea5843e09459ddfae38",
        "end_line": 81,
        "explicit_terminal_LF_map": null,
        "formula": "|E|\\le cS\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\\left|\\frac{\\|u\\|^2-\\|v\\|^2}{2}-\\langle Ku,v\\rangle\\right|\\le\\frac c2S.",
        "literal_BODY_match": true,
        "module_path": "E:/Samplinglib/AutoSamplingTheory/TechnicalLemmas/Analysis/HilbertCorrectorBound.lean",
        "slug": "hilbert-sharp-quadratic-corrector-bound",
        "span_RAW_bytes": 354,
        "span_RAW_sha256": "0b0fe5736aabe70a55a7368aaff5e859c6b702082d780ea5843e09459ddfae38",
        "start_line": 76,
        "step": 5,
        "text": "Both |E| and cS are nonnegative, so their square inequality gives |E|≤cS. The corrector is E/2.",
        "title": "Take the nonnegative square root and divide by two",
        "whole_source_RAW_sha256": "832e68d649c4f6a0c342a476a9d5a7bc5c95d3098abfe41c077cbabc5d51158a"
      },
      {
        "body_start_line": 137,
        "code_RAW_bytes": 6765,
        "code_RAW_sha256": "54a802febc0f0938648067973f1e931d27f2e8d145b5b2efbc19b04d391c44ee",
        "end_line": 299,
        "explicit_terminal_LF_map": null,
        "formula": "H_P^0=\\ker\\langle q_P,\\cdot\\rangle,\\quad\\Gamma_0^{-1}=\\mathrm{Inv},\\quad f_V=V_0^*Rf.",
        "literal_BODY_match": true,
        "module_path": "E:/Samplinglib/AutoSamplingTheory/ExampleCases/ProximalBPS/SharpCorrectorEnergy.lean",
        "slug": "pbps-sharp-corrector-energy",
        "span_RAW_bytes": 6765,
        "span_RAW_sha256": "54a802febc0f0938648067973f1e931d27f2e8d145b5b2efbc19b04d391c44ee",
        "start_line": 138,
        "step": 1,
        "text": "Call the production parent at the unchanged potential and step assumptions; fix the same laws, kernel, centered spaces, inverse and global centered-observable geometry.",
        "title": "Retain the exact actual input and witnesses",
        "whole_source_RAW_sha256": "29225e938479ffb251ed22383d54199f6996543cf57125d925551b8c652fa3bd"
      },
      {
        "body_start_line": 137,
        "code_RAW_bytes": 872,
        "code_RAW_sha256": "5ec3449dbe963b2e1785ccdd90657fa09ce378b7afc587b24ee4ab31cc6776d2",
        "end_line": 315,
        "explicit_terminal_LF_map": null,
        "formula": "K=A_0\\mathrm{Inv}=K^*,\\quad I+K^2=(\\Gamma_0^2+A_0^2)\\mathrm{Inv}^2=\\mathrm{Inv}^2.",
        "literal_BODY_match": true,
        "module_path": "E:/Samplinglib/AutoSamplingTheory/ExampleCases/ProximalBPS/SharpCorrectorEnergy.lean",
        "slug": "pbps-sharp-corrector-energy",
        "span_RAW_bytes": 872,
        "span_RAW_sha256": "5ec3449dbe963b2e1785ccdd90657fa09ce378b7afc587b24ee4ab31cc6776d2",
        "start_line": 300,
        "step": 2,
        "text": "Commuting selfadjoint A0 and Inv give selfadjoint K. Multiply A0²+Γ0²=I by the SAME Inv² and use both inverse identities.",
        "title": "Produce the coefficient identity inside production",
        "whole_source_RAW_sha256": "29225e938479ffb251ed22383d54199f6996543cf57125d925551b8c652fa3bd"
      },
      {
        "body_start_line": 137,
        "code_RAW_bytes": 707,
        "code_RAW_sha256": "4ea2747b71426aca376dc4be9fe3c2d4d99821bea918390c8e9cb2690c0abbb0",
        "end_line": 328,
        "explicit_terminal_LF_map": null,
        "formula": "\\|\\mathrm{Inv}\\|\\le1/\\gamma\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad |C(u,v)|\\le\\frac{\\|u\\|^2+\\|v\\|^2}{2\\gamma}.",
        "literal_BODY_match": true,
        "module_path": "E:/Samplinglib/AutoSamplingTheory/ExampleCases/ProximalBPS/SharpCorrectorEnergy.lean",
        "slug": "pbps-sharp-corrector-energy",
        "span_RAW_bytes": 707,
        "span_RAW_sha256": "4ea2747b71426aca376dc4be9fe3c2d4d99821bea918390c8e9cb2690c0abbb0",
        "start_line": 316,
        "step": 3,
        "text": "Take D=Inv and c=1/γ. Positivity of γ and the existing norm bound discharge all leaf hypotheses without a new public premise.",
        "title": "Apply the sharp Hilbert estimate on the actual centered space",
        "whole_source_RAW_sha256": "29225e938479ffb251ed22383d54199f6996543cf57125d925551b8c652fa3bd"
      },
      {
        "body_start_line": 137,
        "code_RAW_bytes": 1138,
        "code_RAW_sha256": "256c545cd4a5aa1a99c1ffa221266f6e2db8031e1319f18de7578802296069bd",
        "end_line": 351,
        "explicit_terminal_LF_map": null,
        "formula": "\\|f_P\\|^2+\\|f_V\\|^2\\le\\|f\\|^2\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad |C(f_P,f_V)|\\le\\frac{\\|f\\|^2}{2\\gamma}.",
        "literal_BODY_match": true,
        "module_path": "E:/Samplinglib/AutoSamplingTheory/ExampleCases/ProximalBPS/SharpCorrectorEnergy.lean",
        "slug": "pbps-sharp-corrector-energy",
        "span_RAW_bytes": 1138,
        "span_RAW_sha256": "256c545cd4a5aa1a99c1ffa221266f6e2db8031e1319f18de7578802296069bd",
        "start_line": 329,
        "step": 4,
        "text": "Pythagoras and the adjoint contraction give the sum-of-squares budget. Apply the pair bound to the SAME actual fP,fV. An explicitly typed local have proves exactly this final conclusion before the outer witnesses are reconstructed.",
        "title": "Use the actual norm budget",
        "whole_source_RAW_sha256": "29225e938479ffb251ed22383d54199f6996543cf57125d925551b8c652fa3bd"
      },
